        "is_rollback": false,
        "creation_date": 1581364880,
        "post_id": 60157559,
        "post_type": "answer",
        "revision_type": "single_user",
        "revision_number": 1,
        "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "body": "<p><code>jq</code> doesn't have (yet) a <code>printf</code> function to format according locale settings.\nIf that's an option for you can pass the number to the shell using <code>printf</code>:</p>\n<pre><code>echo '{&quot;a&quot;: 12345}' | jq '.a' | xargs printf &quot;%'.f\\n&quot;\n12,345\n</code></pre>\n<p>Note that the printf conversion relies on the format <code>%'.f</code> that is explained in <code>man 3 printf</code></p>\n",
        "revision_guid": "175420A2-B727-4E9F-9533-3A8E38BE64A8"
      }
